Physical: 2x average human!

That's right, Jack had gone from 1.3x straight to 2x from one night's sleep, and Jack felt a limitation that he hadn't before.

'Looks like this is the max amount I can gain naturally just by eating and sleeping after my adaptations.'

'If I want to gain higher natural physical abilities, then I need more adaptations.'

'In the meantime, I can artificially boost my physical abilities by exercising. It should be even more pronounced for me than normal people since my MSTN gene expression is reduced and my body's changes occur ridiculously fast.'

'Let's leave those thoughts for later; for right now I need to get $30 somehow.'

Jack thought as he walked out of the truck stop building. Out of the corner of his eye, he spotted the general store he had noticed when he first arrived in town.

A slow grin crept into Jack's face.

'Apologies to whoever's inside there, I'll pay back the $30 after getting the prize money.'

Jack waited just outside the general store, away from the view of the cashier. After two hours, the cashier went into the back to retrieve something. Jack took this chance to slip inside the store and went straight for a can of bear spray which was behind the counter. Jack thanked god in his mind that black bears were not uncommon in upstate New York.

He hopped the counter as quietly as he could, finding it much easier than he was expecting. Grabbing a can of bear spray, he leapt back and walked out with the most neutral expression he could muster to avoid arousing suspicion from passersby.

Jack's heart thumped loudly.

'Damn, why am I so nervous about stealing even after almost bleeding out to death?'

He walked a good distance away from the store and spotted a bench. Sitting down, he mentally started going over the plan.

'The next one is going to be Alex's 9th kill, meaning he's going to be at the docks tonight. From the movie, only the main dock has a small amount of lights; everything in the periphery will be under pitch darkness, a perfect place for me to hide.'

'Once Alex engages the victim, I'll run in and spray once I'm within 25 feet, which is the range of the spray. I heard it's far more brutal than pepper spray, so I should be able to capture him without a direct fight.'

After confirming his plan, Jack went back to the food court to get something to eat. One of the managers took pity on Jack, seeing as he only had $1.17 to his name left and gave him food worth about $3. 

Jack waited until sunset and made his way to the docks by asking people he passed.

'This should be the spot.'

He looked around the place where the murder was going to take place today. An eerie chill crept up his spine when he thought about the fact that someone was about to die right here.

After scoping the place out, he found some tall bushes nearby that were far enough from the main light while still letting him see everything up close.

It was already pretty dark, and Jack could barely see the bushes; a little bit more time and it'd be pitch black at his hiding place. 

So Jack waited until the sun completely went down. As time passed, Jack became more and more tense, trying to make as little movement as possible. The insects that kept crawling on him didn't make anything better.

Just then, he saw a man walking down to the docks smoking a cigarette.

'That must be the guy about to be killed.'

As the man got closer to the docks, a spark of recognition flickered across Jack's face.

'No fucking shot, that's the guy who gave me a ride when I first got to Raven Hills. What bad luck this guy has.'

But Jack didn't move an inch to warn the guy; he knew this was his one chance to capture Alex alive before the MC from the film takes action.

After the man stared off into the distance towards the water, he suddenly bent forward while tears came out of his eyes.

"WHY! WHY WHY WHYYYYYYY!"

"WHY DID YOU LEAVE ME, SARAH? I DID SO FUCKING MUCH FOR YOU, AND THIS IS HOW YOU REPAY ME!"

'Wow, this part wasn't in the original movie. Getting dumped by his girl, then getting killed by a mass murderer. What a way to go!'

Jack wanted to help him, but he knew the best chance to capture Alex was when he was mid-attack. 

So Jack waited and watched the man cry his heart out until the sound got lower and lower until it was just sniffles. The man stayed slumped, staring into the ground.

After a few more minutes, Jack caught movement off to the side in his peripheral vision. His chest tightened.

'Oh shit, he's here!'

He wanted badly to tell the guy to look out, but he also knew he couldn't miss this chance.

So he watched Alex slowly approach the heartbroken guy from behind, who was still slumped, staring at the ground. Alex gripped the hatchet tighter and lunged, moving his right arm back for a powerful strike.

The man noticed a shadow behind him and looked back, but it was too late; the hatchet was already flying at maximum speed towards the man's abdomen.

Jack knew this was his perfect shot, so he sprang forward from the bushes using all of his strength to run.

Alex noticed him out of the corner of his eye, but he couldn't stop the momentum of the hatchet. It struck deep into the guy's lower abdomen when he let out a bloodcurdling scream.

"AHHHHHHHHHGGGGHGHGHHGHGHGGGGHGG!"

Jack was still running as fast as he could to close the distance.

Alex kicked the guy, dislodging the axe from his abdomen.

But Jack had made it; he was already within 20 feet of Alex.

He had already pulled the plastic lock off before; he now aimed the bear spray at Alex and pressed the trigger.

A mass of brown mist shot forward at extreme speeds, reaching Alex before he could connect the dots on what was happening.

Alex immediately started screaming like he was dying. But his screaming was cut short as he started choking and thrashing around on the floor, his eyes and nose starting to become red. But worst of all, his eyes were swollen shut.

He had taken bear spray directly to the face; he was going to be completely incapacitated for a good several minutes, and his blindness could last a lot longer.

However, Jack stopped and took a few steps back. Even for the tiny amounts Jack was exposed to, he felt his lungs, eyes, lips and nose burning. He couldn't imagine how bad Alex had it as he took a direct shot and was still in the bear spray mist. 

Unfortunately, the guy Alex attacked was also subjected to some of the bear spray, as they have a wide range. Fortunately, he was far enough away to crawl away from the mist before too much damage was done. But he still had a massive wound from the hatchet strike, bleeding far too fast to stop.

Jack ran over.

"HEY, HOLD ON, GIVE ME YOUR PHONE, I'M CALLING THE POLICE."

Jack dialled 911 while holding the wounded area tight with his shirt.

"911, where is your emergency?"

"Docks. West Side. Someone's bleeding like crazy and the Shepherd of Blood is incapacitated."

After a couple more back-and-forth with the cops, Jack tried to keep pressure on the man's wound, but he got drowsier and drowsier before passing out. 

Alex seemed to be choking less now, but he was still blind, though.

‘Yeah, I ain't taking any chances.’

Jack also sprayed some more bear spray on Alex to make sure he stayed down. The cops arrived shortly after.

Alex and the man were both taken to the hospital, except Alex was in restraints. And Jack was taken to the police station to give his testimony and statement.

[Police Station]

Jack was checked for injuries, cleaned, and given some water. He waited in one of the rooms for the officers to get situated and question him about the situation.

‘Most of the questions they ask, I can probably be truthful about.’

‘But there are minor holes in my story as well.’

‘Well, I can always just refuse to talk since I’m not the assailant, but that might bring more suspicion on me.’

Jack snapped out of his thoughts as the door was pushed open to reveal an officer and a lady.

The officer started speaking.

“First of all, on behalf of everyone in Raven Hills, thank you for stepping up to save Charlie and capture the attacker.”

“No problem, everything was happening very fast, so my body just kinda moved.”

‘So his name’s Charlie, huh? Might be less suspicious if I act like I’m worried about him.’

Jack put on a pained and worried expression to the best of his abilities.

“Also, is Charlie going to be okay? His injury looked pretty serious!”

“He’s currently in the ICU; hopefully he’ll be fine.”

The lady started speaking.

“Right now, we need to gather as much information as possible.”

“We ask that you answer our questions with as much detail as possible.”

“Of course, officers, I wanna help as much as I can. Ask away!”

It started with basic questions about who he was, if he knew Charlie, and what he was doing in Raven Hills. Jack gave the cops the same spiel that he gave to Charlie the first time they met. But then the officers asked about him being homeless.

‘Man, I don’t even know my past; what am I supposed to tell you? If I make something up and they have records of me doing something else, then I'm cooked!’

“Haha, I’m not really comfortable speaking about that, you know how it is.”

“We’re all here for Charlie and Alex anyway, so let's start that part.”

‘FUCKKKK, I’M NOT SUPPOSED TO KNOW WHO ALEX IS, WHY DID I MENTION HIM? It’s fine, It’s fine, I don't think they’ll catch it though.’

“Fair enough, it's just some basic background info, but we can skip that one if you aren't comfortable.”

Thankfully, the officers didn’t catch Jack’s slip of the tongue and asked what exactly happened, which Jack answered truthfully. Inwardly, though, Jack was relieved and steeled himself to speak cautiously so it wouldn’t happen again.

Finally, the main question he had been preparing the lies for came.

“So why were you at the docks hiding?”

“I wasn’t actually trying to hide at first.”

“I like looking at lakes or oceans to clear my mind.”

“But I heard a guy crying off on the other side, so I went to check it out.”

“I thought it’d be too awkward if I just went up to him.”

“But I’m kind of a nosy person, haha, so I hid in one of the bushes when I heard him screaming about a breakup.”

“A few minutes later, the assailant showed up.”

“At first I thought he went up to Charlie to comfort him, but he took a large swing with his axe towards him, and you know the rest.”

“I see, and why did you have bear spray on you?”

“Like I said during the background questions, I usually hike a lot, so carrying bear spray to deter a potential bear or moose is a must. Although luckily I haven’t encountered a bear.”

“Well, you do look like a hiker, more buff than a normal hiker!”

“Haha, thanks, I usually try to take care of my health.”

‘Ha, I haven’t even exercised once; this shit’s just the base adaptations.’

After that, another hour passed of minor questions and chit-chat, which Jack didn’t have to lie about, and it looked like the questioning was finally coming to an end.

“Alright, Mr Sterbin, I think that's all the questions we had for you.”

“We thank you very much for your cooperation.”

“No problem. If anything else pops up that needs my help, then please do let me know! I’ve always wanted to be one of the boys in blue.”

‘Ha, who's helping you? I’m gonna be outta this town as soon as I get the money.’

“Also, I don’t mean to be insensitive, but I was wondering when I’d get the capture reward for the Shepherd of Blood.”

“It’s just that, you know that I’m homeless, so it’s hard for me to get money for food and shelter.”

“Well, technically, Alex is still a suspect until he goes to court, even though there’s an overwhelming amount of evidence against him.”

“But fortunately for you, the people who offered the reward on the Shepherd of Blood aren’t directly related to the police department. It’s a group formed from the victims' families, so they don’t need to wait for an official hearing with this amount of evidence.”

“However, it is deep into the night right now, so I don’t think they’re awake.”

“ I’m sure you can go once the sun is up to collect your reward!”

“If you need a place to stay for the night, then I can do you a favour and let you use a spare room since you’ve been so cooperative.”

“Thank you very much, officers. I’ll go with your arrangement.”

